│ Immediate-Mode REPL: TODO Implementation Plan                                                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Context                                                                                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ The OpenGL immediate-mode REPL (sample.c, ~5,763 lines) is a live C-based command interpreter for fixed-function OpenGL. Users type GL commands in a left-panel editor and see results rendered in a 3D │
│ viewport. The codebase uses a two-array architecture (g_cmds[] raw → g_flat_cmds[] expanded) with a PC-based executor designed for future flow control. This plan addresses 10 TODO items grouped into 4│
│  phases.                                                                                                                                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Critical files:                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ - sample.c — main app, all 10 items touch this                                                                                                                                                          │
│ - repl_eval.c / repl_eval.h — expression evaluator (no changes needed, read-only reference)                                                                                                             │
│ - include/gl_includes.h — already includes GLU                                                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ ---                                                                                                                                                                                                     │
│ Phase 1: Bug Fixes & Low-Risk Improvements                                                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ 1. Fix lighting default state bug                                                                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Problem: GL_LIGHTING gets re-enabled by end_2d() (line ~1964) and overlay restore paths in render_3d_scene() even when the user hasn't typed glEnable(GL_LIGHTING).                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Fix:                                                                                                                                                                                                    │
│ - Add g_user_lighting_enabled flag (default 0)                                                                                                                                                          │
│ - During flatten_commands(), scan for any CMD_ENABLE with GL_LIGHTING to set the flag                                                                                                                   │
│ - In render_3d_scene(), before execute_commands(): glDisable(GL_LIGHTING) as baseline                                                                                                                   │
│ - Change all lighting restore paths (end_2d(), post-overlay code) to check g_user_lighting_enabled before calling glEnable(GL_LIGHTING)                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ 2. Fix output.c generation for functions                                                                                                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Problem: save_output() has no cases for CMD_FUNC_DEF, CMD_FUNC_END, CMD_CALL — they fall through to default which emits invalid C.                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Fix (two-pass approach):                                                                                                                                                                                │
│ - Pass 1: Before the display function body, scan g_cmds[] for CMD_FUNC_DEF blocks. Emit each as static void funcN(void) { ... } with body commands translated to C                                      │
│ - Pass 2: In the snippet section, skip CMD_FUNC_DEF..CMD_FUNC_END blocks; emit CMD_CALL as funcN();                                                                                                     │
│ - Split g_header_pre to allow inserting function definitions between includes and display()                                                                                                             │
│ - Reuse existing write_for_begin_as_c() and expression translation for body commands                                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ 3. Improve vertex entry plane preview                                                                                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Problem: When typing glVertex3f(x',y',_) with 2 args, only a Z-line is drawn. Should also show the XZ plane at y=y'.                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
│ Fix: In draw_vertex_guides() (line ~3153), modify the n == 2 case:                                                                                                                                      │
│ - Draw a semi-transparent XZ plane quad at y=y' (the known second arg)                                                                                                                                  │
│ - Keep the existing Z-line at (x',y') for precision                                                                                                                                                     │
│ - Add plane outline for visibility                                                                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                                                                         │
